{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793624139,"nonce":"Psn8qRkFfX6qzYcEebliM7IYTvg=","title":"Text input: stylesheet rules beat the builder's colour setters","message":"TextInputConfig's colours (text, placeholder, caret, selection) are set by the builder (text_color, placeholder_color, cursor_color, selection_color) and then overwritten by apply_css_overrides whenever a matching rule sets the same property. Inline styles should win over the stylesheet, as they do on a Div.\n\nConsequence: cn::input cannot put its colour defaults in .cn-input rules (color, caret-color, ::placeholder, ::selection) without breaking a caller's InputBuilder::text_color(..) and friends, so it leaves them to the widget's theme defaults. Fix by recording which config fields the builder set and skipping CSS for those.","files":null}]}